# ECO JOURNAL app — .gitignore (LAB, Phase 1 setup)
# Intent: the repo must be pushable as-is with zero secrets in it.
# edge/out/ is INTENTIONALLY committed: GitHub Pages serves the
# committed snapshot (CI does not regenerate it — the source
# database is not in this repo; regeneration happens in the lab).

# Android / Gradle build outputs
.gradle/
build/
app/build/
*.apk
*.aab

# Local SDK / IDE config
local.properties
*.iml
.idea/
*.DS_Store

# Signing keys — NEVER commit. Release signing is a separate,
# later decision by Yasin, with a key he creates himself.
*.jks
*.keystore

# Firebase — supplied later by the owner, NEVER committed.
# The app compiles and runs without it (FCM is optional at runtime;
# see docs/firebase-setup.md).
google-services.json
app/google-services.json

# Secrets of any kind
*.env
*.pem
*.key

# Lab dry-run bridge state — scratch only, NOT the production
# sent-record. See bridge/dryrun.py.
bridge/.dryrun-state/
